{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language canonicalisation fixture for runback.cassette/v1.",
    "",
    "`canonical` is what packages/verify/index.js produces — the reference",
    "implementation — and every other implementation MUST produce it byte for",
    "byte. Regenerate with: node packages/verify/testdata/generate.mjs",
    "",
    "This exists because three implementations had already drifted without",
    "anything noticing: each was tested, and each passed, because each was",
    "tested against itself. Divergences measured when it was written:",
    "",
    "  Python  1e-7  -> \"1e-07\"     exponent padded to two digits",
    "  Python  1e16  -> \"1e+16\"     sci notation from 1e16 instead of 1e21",
    "  Python  non-BMP keys ordered by code point, not UTF-16 code unit",
    "  Go      < > & -> \\u003c ...  encoding/json's HTML-escaping default",
    "  Go      U+2028/9 escaped even under SetEscapeHTML(false)",
    "  Go      non-BMP keys ordered by UTF-8 byte, not UTF-16 code unit",
    "",
    "Each produces a different digest for the same record — one implementation",
    "calling TAMPERED what another calls VALID. For a format whose whole claim",
    "is 'verify this without us', that is the product failing, not a helper.",
    "",
    "The vectors are deliberately nasty. Ordinary data agreed all along, which",
    "is exactly why the drift survived."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "html-sensitive characters are NOT escaped",
      "value": {
        "a": "<b>&</b>"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"<b>&</b>\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "U+2028 and U+2029 stay raw",
      "value": {
        "a": "x y z"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"x y z\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "small exponent is not zero-padded",
      "value": {
        "a": 1e-7
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":1e-7}"
    },
    {
      "name": "scientific notation starts at 1e21, not 1e16",
      "value": {
        "a": 10000000000000000
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":10000000000000000}"
    },
    {
      "name": "1e21 is the first exponential",
      "value": {
        "a": 1e+21
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":1e+21}"
    },
    {
      "name": "1e-6 is still positional",
      "value": {
        "a": 0.000001
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":0.000001}"
    },
    {
      "name": "negative zero prints as zero",
      "value": {
        "a": 0
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":0}"
    },
    {
      "name": "non-BMP keys sort by UTF-16 code unit",
      "value": {
        "😀": 1,
        "�": 2
      },
      "canonical": "{\"😀\":1,\"�\":2}"
    },
    {
      "name": "integer-like keys sort as strings",
      "value": {
        "2": "b",
        "10": "a",
        "x": "c"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"10\":\"a\",\"2\":\"b\",\"x\":\"c\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "quote and backslash",
      "value": {
        "a": "\"\\"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"\\\"\\\\\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "control characters: short forms, then \\u00XX",
      "value": {
        "a": "\u0001\b\t\n\f\r\u001f"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"\\u0001\\b\\t\\n\\f\\r\\u001f\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "whole floats lose the decimal point",
      "value": {
        "a": 1,
        "b": 100
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":1,\"b\":100}"
    },
    {
      "name": "large magnitude",
      "value": {
        "a": 1.5e+300
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":1.5e+300}"
    },
    {
      "name": "fractional round-trip",
      "value": {
        "a": 0.1,
        "b": 2.5,
        "c": 1.2345678901234567
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":0.1,\"b\":2.5,\"c\":1.2345678901234567}"
    },
    {
      "name": "nested objects sort at every level",
      "value": {
        "b": [
          1,
          {
            "z": null,
            "a": true
          }
        ],
        "a": "x"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"x\",\"b\":[1,{\"a\":true,\"z\":null}]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "empty containers",
      "value": {
        "a": {},
        "b": []
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":{},\"b\":[]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "non-ascii values stay raw",
      "value": {
        "a": "café → 日本 🎉"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"café → 日本 🎉\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "booleans and null",
      "value": {
        "t": true,
        "f": false,
        "n": null
      },
      "canonical": "{\"f\":false,\"n\":null,\"t\":true}"
    },
    {
      "name": "top-level array",
      "value": [
        3,
        "a",
        null,
        true
      ],
      "canonical": "[3,\"a\",null,true]"
    },
    {
      "name": "key ordering is by code unit, not locale",
      "value": {
        "Z": 1,
        "a": 2,
        "B": 3
      },
      "canonical": "{\"B\":3,\"Z\":1,\"a\":2}"
    },
    {
      "name": "surrogate pair inside a value",
      "value": {
        "a": "💩"
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":\"💩\"}"
    },
    {
      "name": "deeply nested",
      "value": {
        "a": {
          "b": {
            "c": {
              "d": [
                1,
                [
                  2,
                  [
                    3
                  ]
                ]
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "canonical": "{\"a\":{\"b\":{\"c\":{\"d\":[1,[2,[3]]]}}}}"
    }
  ]
}
